# A list has its length as a property of its own that no accessor can be laid over: the store of a whole number from nought up runs no code of the program. It is an operation of its own and has no site.
# A program restores or trims a list to a length that it mostly has already: then nothing is stored.
# f1 = restore, f2 = storeAnyNumber, f3 = emptyInTurns
